Tamara McKay is a female elf in high-ranking security armor who usually keeps her face masked, though her movements are so fluid and relaxed they communicate everything a face would. If she unmasks, a couple of distinct, elegant dueling scars mark her jaw.

Tamara is a member of [[Org/Protectorate/index|Protectorate]].

She travels with a gnomish companion, both of them masked. At the [[Geography/Færrin/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]] pilgrimage the pair hunt keystone 8, which she means the Protectorate to have. She turned down [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]]'s offer of an alliance and a seat in the Party's car; she and her companion mean to bring their own friends once they hold the keystone.

She drills the Protectorate's junior members in the fane's sandpit, taking on five or more at once with no weapon of her own, breaking bones and then setting and healing them for the next round.

She was left with [[Org/Protectorate/People/Yao Addington|Yao]] to hold the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid 3|Hesperid 3]] works while the Party went on to the wreck, and she met their train on its return at gunpoint, wary that the four of them had been taken. She took charge of the questioning, had the Sedecium survivors guarded in the train by Yao rather than by any of the Party, and told the Party afterward that she would rather throw her lot in with them than take her chances with [[Org/Amber Call/People/Silven Grayson|Grayson]]. She says the [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] can keep a secret and that the Party should not tell [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/People/Hildebrandt|Hildebrandt]]. She means to be in on the killing of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]].
